git -C $csrbt commit -m "ADR-205: a page with no outputs is not measured by the audit that measures outputs" `
  -m "Two pages of this kit accepted TWENTY-NINE and NINETEEN typed values apiece -- a haemocytometer count with its Poisson CV, a passage log with cumulative population doublings, a four-point standard curve and an unknown read off it, plate counts with TFTC/TNTC judgements, an exponential growth fit, disc-diffusion zones -- and offered NO WAY TO GET ANY OF IT OUT. Not a copy button, not a CSV, not a print block. audit_outputs walks every page, finds the controls whose name says they hand something over, presses each and asks what came out; it has one line in it -- ``if not r.get(`"buttons`"): continue`` -- which means THE ONE PAGE SHAPE IT EXISTS TO CATCH is the one shape it cannot report. Not as '0 held of 0': as nothing at all. The kit's total read '3 of 75 outputs leave a page with nothing reading them' and was true, and the two worst pages in the kit were not in the denominator. THE ABSENCE OF A ROW IS THE LOUDEST THING A LEDGER CAN SAY, and this one was saying it into a wall. THE EXPORTS: both benches gain the kit's convention, an Export pane with a bench sheet and a CSV per log, copied through one copyText that marks on the clipboard's answer rather than the click (ADR-203). THE SHEET CARRIES THE INPUTS BESIDE THE RESULTS -- a concentration without its chamber factor and dilution, a doubling time without the interval, an unknown without the standards it was read off are each a number nobody downstream can check, and a sheet of answers alone would make the page a WORSE record than a notebook. AND IT CARRIES THE WARNINGS: where the page refused a reading on screen -- an absorbance off the end of the standards, a plate outside the countable window, points above OD 0.6 in an exponential fit -- the sheet says so IN THE LINE, because a caveat that lives only on a screen the reader has closed was never given. EVERY PLATE IS CARRIED, INCLUDING THE REJECTED ONES, marked TFTC or TNTC, since a CFU/mL reported without the plates that were excluded is a count nobody can audit. AND A ZONE CARRIES ITS BREAKPOINT SOURCE, because that page ships no breakpoint table on purpose and an export that dropped the source would undo that refusal on the way out of the tab. A CSV IS AN INSTRUMENT READING, NOT A FLOAT DUMP: the first plate CSV handed out 147999999.99999997 for a plate the page displays as 1.480e+8, eleven significant figures from a hundred and forty-eight colonies, and every derived column is now written at the precision the screen shows -- caught by pinning the CSV in the page's task, which is the point of pinning it. THE RULE, SO IT CANNOT HAPPEN AGAIN: the skip is gone; a page with no output button gets a row and a judgement -- under FOUR entry controls it passes quietly, because a glossary with a search box is not a data trap and a rule that named every page without an export would be switched off within a week; at or above four it must hand something over or be DECLARED WITH A REASON in the ledger. What counts as an entry control is read from harness.TYPED rather than restated, so a kind added tomorrow counts tomorrow -- the ADR-141 rule this whole slice is an instance of. AND THE EXPORTS ARE HELD, NOT JUST PRESENT: both science tasks press every new button and read what came out, with the bench sheet pinned against the figures each task's existing oracle already holds -- 6.000x10^5 live cells/mL, 90.9% viability, a 16.00 h doubling time, a cumulative PD of 4.0, 9.900x10^7 CFU/mL from two countable plates of three. THE KIT IS NOW AT 0 OF 75 OUTPUTS THAT NOTHING READS, both ceilings at zero. verify_outputs 26 -> 38 with TWO new fixtures (a trap, and a page that is RIGHT to hand nothing over -- the check that the quiet page is NOT named carries as much weight as the check that the trap is); mutate_outputs 24 -> 31, all killed; two new routes. STILL FILED: neither bench keeps your work, so a tab closed mid-session still loses everything -- the next slice, and only possible now; and the bar is a COUNT, not an understanding." `
  -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>" -m "Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YPcb1A7CejriRgL9xLrhJ3"
